-- Unreleased (after V6.5.1)

- fix: The panel's Playtime tile shows the two largest units, such as "2d, 23h". The full "2d, 23h, 59m, 48s" wrapped onto a second line and was cut off. `!time` in chat still shows every unit

-- 2026.10.31 - V6.5.1

- fix: Panel tabs, captions, buttons and pop-up titles no longer show a dotted capital İ ("MİSSİONS", "ACHİEVEMENTS") for players whose CS2 runs in Turkish. CS2 capitalized these with the player's game language; K4 now sends them already capitalized in the player's K4 language, so English reads "MISSIONS" and Turkish keeps its own capitals
- fix: All progress bars on the Missions and Achievements tabs are the same length; a long progress text such as "1,227/10,000 · +2,500" made its bar shorter
- setup: Needs the updated Workshop addon `3811667212`. A 6.5.0 server with the new addon shows these labels in normal case instead of capitals until it is updated; nothing else changes. No config, language or database changes

-- 2026.10.31 - Workshop addon update (after V6.5.0)

- fix: The addon's rank emblems are now exact copies of the current CS2 ones. 11 of them (skillgroup 1, 11, 12, 13, 17, 18 and wingman 11, 12, 13, 17, 18) were from an older version of Valve's artwork, and all 38 carried invisible leftover shapes. Checked against the installed game: every one of the 123 images the panel uses exists in CS2 or ships in the addon
- chore: `panorama/tools/check_game_images.py` checks the addon against an installed CS2, and `gen_k4_ranks.py` now reads the emblems straight from the game's `pak01_dir.vpk` (no Source2Viewer needed)
- setup: Republish Workshop addon `3811667212`. The server plugin did not change; servers stay on 6.5.0

-- 2026.10.31 - V6.5.0

- feat: Achievements. 21 long-term goals, from 100 kills and 10 hours played to a 30-day mission streak, each unlocking once with one-time points (and an optional server command). Progress comes from the stats, playtime and streak K4 already stores. Goals a player had already reached unlock without the reward, so the update does not hand out points for old history. `!achievements` shows progress; everyone sees unlocks in chat. Edit `plugins/K4-System/achievements.jsonc`, names in all 36 languages. Settings: `modules.achievements`, `commands.achievements`. New table `k4achievements`, created automatically
- feat: The panel gets an Achievements tab (four cards per page, the closest to done first, unlocked ones after) and a gold line under the header while a points event is on. Unlocked achievements and starting events show as pop-ups. Needs the updated Workshop addon; servers and players on the old addon keep working, they just do not see the new tab and line
- setup: Workshop addon `3811667212` must be republished from `panorama/k4system` for the new tab and event line (pop-ups already work with the current addon)
- feat: Points events. Schedule more points for playing at set times in `events.schedule`, such as 2× on weekend evenings, or start one any time with `css_k4_event 2 60` (`css_k4_event stop` ends it). Kills, rounds, objectives and playtime points are multiplied; mission rewards, bounties, duels and point losses are not. Everyone is told when an event starts and ends, players who join during one are told too, and the panel shows a pop-up. The schedule is empty by default
- feat: Anti-farming, on by default. A kill between two players on the same connection gives and takes no points, so a second account cannot feed the first. After 10 kills on the same player within 10 minutes, each further kill on them is worth 25% of the points (and costs them 25%), and the point message says so. Normal matches never reach the limit. Settings: `anti-farm`
- fix: With `ranks.dynamic-death-points` on, a victim with 0 points was worth full kill points instead of the lowest multiplier, which made an empty second account the best one to farm
- feat: Point history for admins. Every manual point change is logged with the time, the change, the new total and who did it: admin point commands, admin and personal resets, and other plugins through the shared API. `css_k4_history <target|steamid64> [count]` shows the newest entries, also for offline players. Kept for 90 days. New table `k4pointlog`, created automatically
- feat: `css_k4_reload` applies changes to `k4-system.jsonc`, `ranks.jsonc`, `missions.jsonc` and `achievements.jsonc` without a restart. It reads them all first, and when one has a problem it names it and reloads nothing, so a typo can no longer leave the server without K4
- fix: The 5.x upgrade guard (K4 waits until the new `k4-system.jsonc` is filled in when an old `K4-System.json` exists) now compares values, not text, so an untouched file written by an older 6.x still counts as untouched after this update
- fix: Any death now ends the killer's streak, also one that gives no points (such as a bot kill with `tracking.count-bots` off). Before, the streak bonuses kept growing in long deathmatch rounds
- fix: With `ranks.round-summary` on, points from a round in which tracking stopped (a player left and the server fell below `tracking.minimum-players`) are summarized instead of silently added
- fix: Stats no longer count a round win or loss for a player who joined a team seconds before the round ended, the same rule round points already used
- fix: A free-for-all match in which no player got a kill has no winner, instead of a match win for an arbitrary player
- fix: Duels open again after `mp_match_end_restart` or `mp_restartgame` on the same map; before, every `!duel` said "not now" until the map changed
- fix: Accepting a duel checks the 10% stake limit again, so a player whose points dropped after the challenge cannot stake more than allowed
- fix: When K4 reloads during a duel and one player has already left, the player still here gets both stakes, as at the match end; before, the leaver's stake was lost
- fix: Custom `WeaponKills` missions for knives and grenades were swapped away on every map. Knife missions are now possible everywhere, grenade missions where grenades are, and `planted_c4` where there is a bomb
- fix: `!resetdata`, `!setpoints`, `!givepoints` and `!removepoints` refuse a plain name that matches several players (such as "jo") and say how many it matched. `#userid` and groups such as `@ct` still work
- fix: `!resetmydata all` no longer starts the 24-hour rank-reset cooldown when the ranks module is off
- fix: A broken placeholder in your own language line (`configs/plugins/K4-System/lang/`), such as `{name}` or `{3}` on a line with fewer values, shows the shipped text instead of breaking the command
- fix: A command name listed twice in one list ran its command twice; it is now used once, with a warning in the console
- fix: Other plugins reading the shared API (points, rank, placement) from a background thread no longer read K4's player list or the game there, which could fail or crash
- fix: Purging inactive players runs in one transaction, so a player who joins during the purge cannot lose only their stats and playtime
- fix: Two plugin reloads in a row no longer skip waiting for the first instance's unfinished saves
- perf: The player count behind every shot, hit and kill is read from the game at most every half second instead of on every event, which was the hottest path on full servers
- perf: The panel caches leaderboard and rank data even while the player keeps clicking, and `!top` saves all players at most every 10 seconds for the whole server, so clicking and `!top` spam can no longer flood the database
- fix: A `ranks.playtime-reward.every-minutes` value above one week (10080) is capped; a huge value threw an error on every timer tick
- setup: Existing config files get every new setting with its default and need no changes. New sections to change them: `anti-farm`, `events`, `modules.achievements`, `commands.achievements`. New texts in all 36 languages. New tables `k4pointlog` and `k4achievements` are created on the next start; existing tables are not changed

-- 2026.10.29 - V6.4.0

- feat: Bounties. A player who gets 7 kills on real players in one life becomes WANTED: everyone sees it in chat (and as a pop-up with the panel), and the enemy who ends the streak gets +150 points. The wanted player loses nothing extra. A wanted player who is never caught gets +50 when the match ends. Only one player is wanted at a time, and each player at most once per map, so it stays rare. Settings: `bounty`
- feat: Duels. `!duel <player> <points>` challenges a player; they answer with `!duel accept` or `!duel decline` within 30 seconds. Both stakes are held, and whoever gets more kills from then until the match ends takes both. A tie returns the stakes, and a player who has left when the match ends loses. Each player can duel once per map, the stake is at most 10% of the poorer player's points, and players on the same connection cannot duel each other, so points cannot be moved between accounts. Settings: `duels`, command names: `commands.duel`
- feat: The panel's Rank tab shows who is wanted, your running duel with the kill score, and a challenge waiting for you with Accept and Decline buttons. With nothing going on, it shows a short hint. Needs the updated Workshop addon; servers and players on the old addon keep working, they just do not see these lines
- change: The panel header no longer shows the K4 icon and "K4" text; the player's name starts the header (Workshop addon)
- change: Panel polish (Workshop addon): the player's name is the header title, the active tab is underlined, boxes and rows get a fine border, the rank progress bar is thicker, "to go" is in the accent color, leaderboard rows alternate shades, stat numbers are larger, finished missions get a green border, and Accept is highlighted next to Decline
- setup: Both are on by default and need the ranks module. Existing config files get the defaults without changes; add the `bounty` and `duels` sections to change them. New texts in all 36 languages. No database changes

-- 2026.10.22 - V6.3.3

- fix: Playtime counted the time a player survived a round as dead time. CS2 respawns survivors at every round start, and each of those spawns added the round to "dead"; alive and dead time are now split correctly
- fix: Points set by another plugin through the shared API from a background thread no longer read K4's player list on that thread, which could fail or crash. The whole change now runs on the game thread
- fix: Damage missions no longer over-count a kill after fall damage, bot damage or team damage: the killing hit counts only the health the victim still had
- fix: With `ranks.round-summary` on, points after the round summary (MVP, exit frags) get their own message instead of showing up in the next round's summary or not at all
- fix: A server that still has the old 5.x `K4-System.json` keeps refusing to track until the new `k4-system.jsonc` is filled in, also after a second restart, so it never runs on an empty database by mistake
- docs: README brought up to date: panel behavior without the addon, purge of inactive players after 30 days, mission settings, admin and console commands, updating steps, building from source, and Valve artwork credit
- chore: Repository moved to GitHub (https://github.com/karola3vax/K4-System) with releases built by GitHub Actions; cleaned-up ignore rules, line endings and issue templates
- setup: No config, language or database changes

-- 2026.10.22 - V6.3.2

- change: With `commands.rank-to-everyone` on, `!rank` posts only the one public line, which the player sees too, like LVL Ranks. The player's own rank block is no longer sent as well
- feat: The console warns at startup about command names that cannot work: a name with a comma or space in it (such as `"k4, lvl"` instead of `"k4", "lvl"`), and a name that is in two command lists, which runs both commands at once
- setup: No config, language or database changes

-- 2026.10.21 - V6.3.1

- feat: `ranks.round-summary` now shows what the round's points came from: after the total, one line per reason, such as "5× Kill: +100" and "2× Headshot: +10" (Quinella's request). A round with only one reason keeps the single line
- change: With `commands.rank-to-everyone` on, `!rank` only posts the line to chat and no longer opens the panel, like LVL Ranks. `!k4` still opens the panel on the Rank tab
- feat: `commands.main` sets the names of the main command (`!k4` by default), so `!lvl` can open the panel for players used to LVL Ranks: `"main": ["k4", "lvl"]` (Quinella's request)
- setup: No language or database changes. `commands.main` is optional; without it, `!k4` works as before

-- 2026.10.14 - V6.3.0

- feat: Missions follow the map. K4 reads every map (bomb sites, hostages, game mode, respawns, free-for-all, what the buy menu sells, and the weapons players carry or use) and only gives missions that can be done there: no grenade missions on aim maps, no rifle missions on AWP maps, no round or clutch missions in deathmatch, no bomb plants in Retakes
- feat: An untouched mission that does not fit the current map is swapped for free for one that does, with a chat message; it does not use the daily reroll. A started one is kept and marked "not on this map", so it can be finished elsewhere
- feat: `missions.map-rules` corrects maps K4 reads wrong, by map name pattern (`aim_*`, `awp_*` are set by default): rounds, bomb, hostages, grenades, the only weapons, and mission types to never give
- feat: One weekly mission next to the three daily ones. It resets on Monday at midnight, pays `missions.rewards.weekly` (2500), shows its time left, and does not count for the daily streak. Add or remove `Weekly` missions in `missions.jsonc`; without any, there is no weekly mission
- feat: 18 new mission types: wallbang, through-smoke, in-air, while-flashed, long-range, Zeus and revenge kills; pistol, SMG, shotgun, rifle and sniper kills; opening kills, clutch wins, kills in one round, kills in one life, surviving rounds, and damage dealt
- feat: The default list grows from 24 to 54 missions, including 8 weekly ones. A `missions.jsonc` that was never edited is updated automatically; an edited one is left alone
- feat: The panel shows the weekly mission as a fourth card, dims missions that are not possible on the current map, and uses CS2's kill-feed markers as icons for the new kill missions
- setup: The fourth card and the new icons are in the Workshop addon `3811667212`, already updated; players and servers get it automatically
- setup: No database changes. The weekly mission is stored in the existing missions table

