- fix: K4's panel no longer blocks the mouse for other plugins' menus (their hover effects and sounds work again while K4 runs). Already delivered through the Workshop addon `3811667212` on 2026-10-08
- setup: The new line is `rank.public` (and `rank.public-points` without stats) in the language files; change it in `configs/plugins/K4-System/lang/` to keep your wording through updates

-- 2026.10.04 - V6.2.2

- fix: K4 starts on older MySQL servers again. MySQL before 5.6.5 refused the rank rewards table (a date column defaulted to the current time), and every table after it, such as the rank resets and missions tables, was then never created
- fix: A table the database refuses no longer stops the other tables from being created; the console names the table and the database's reason
- fix: The rank rewards index fits servers without large index prefixes (767 bytes)
- fix: Panel toasts (promotions, finished missions, streak bonus) appear at the right side, vertically centred, instead of over the kill feed in the top right corner
- feat: Your own wording survives updates. Put only the lines you change in `configs/plugins/K4-System/lang/<language>.json` (for example `en.json`); they win over the shipped text, and every other line keeps the shipped text. Updates never touch that folder, so there is nothing to redo after pasting a new release. K4 creates the folder with a short how-to file, and names any file it can't read in the console
- setup: Existing databases need nothing; the missing tables are created on the next start
- setup: Edited `plugins/K4-System/lang` files? Copy just the lines you changed into `configs/plugins/K4-System/lang/` once; after that, updates can replace the `lang` folder freely
