-- 2026.10.01 - V6.0.0

- rewrite: Rebuild K4-System from scratch with the same features, commands, permissions, database tables, and shared API
- breaking: Replace the config with one commented file, `configs/plugins/K4-System/k4-system.jsonc`, with grouped sections and consistent names. 5.x configs are not migrated; K4 stops with clear instructions until the new file is filled in. See the README upgrade table
- feat: Add point presets (`casual`, `competitive`, `deathmatch`) with per-value overrides; `casual` equals the 5.x defaults
- changed: Merge the separate rank and stat settings for minimum players, warmup, and bots into one `tracking` section, and drop `load-messages`
- changed: Default to SQLite storage, real CounterStrikeSharp admin permissions for the example admin tags, and a short `#15` top-placement tag for the top 100
- breaking: Rewrite all chat messages with a shorter, consistent style and new key names, and retranslate all languages from the new English; custom language files must be redone
- feat: Localize the rank menu title and add a header to the top list
- feat: Add 23 languages: Arabic, Azerbaijani, Bulgarian, Danish, Dutch, Estonian, Finnish, Greek, Hungarian, Indonesian, Japanese, Kazakh, Korean, Lithuanian, Norwegian, Polish, European Portuguese, Serbian, Slovak, Swedish, Thai, Traditional Chinese, and Vietnamese (36 in total)
- fix: Send every message in the language each player chose with `!lang`. Point messages, promotions, `!rank` and `!top` results, the rank menu, and announcements always used the server language before
- changed: Reject unknown or misspelled config settings with a message that names them
- feat: Add SQLite storage, used by default; the database file is `plugins/K4-System/k4system.db`. Set `storage.type` to `mysql` for MySQL
- compatibility: Update K4-System, K4-SharedApi, and tests to CounterStrikeSharp.API 1.0.376 and require runtime API 376
- compatibility: Existing MySQL databases and ranks.jsonc files load unchanged
- performance: Never block the game thread on the database while loading, and save all player data from one background writer
- performance: Look players up directly instead of copying the player list for every event and every tick
- performance: Bind SteamIDs as text so MySQL uses the primary key, and add a points index for leaderboard positions
- reliability: Wait only for the joining player's own unsaved data before loading them, instead of every pending task
- reliability: Keep K4-granted rank permissions removable after a map change, and drop players who left during a map change
- reliability: Run a reward command at most once per session even when saving its completion fails
- fix: Release rank permissions of a player whose slot is taken over after a map change, so they cannot stay granted until restart
- fix: Discard a reward claim that finishes after the player's personal rank reset, so it cannot run later for a rank they no longer hold
- fix: Stop re-checking already delivered rewards every round, and retry a player load that failed instead of leaving them untracked for the map
- reliability: Bound the final save on unload to 15 seconds instead of waiting forever
- changed: Read ranks.jsonc with System.Text.Json; comments, trailing commas, any property-name casing, and points written as text or as 500.0 still work. Newtonsoft.Json is no longer shipped
- changed: Retry unfinished rank rewards at round start and on join instead of after every kill
- changed: Command cooldown messages show the seconds actually remaining
- fix: Add the missing space between a point message and the attacker or victim name
- db: Add a `k4schema` table that records applied database upgrades
- ci: Make GitLab the only home: remove the GitHub release workflow and move the issue templates to GitLab
- test: Replace the console gate with an xUnit suite of 204 tests, including SQLite and MySQL storage tests and a 5.0 database upgrade test

